        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(media): keep host-staged images available to native vision",
        "body": "Closes #106408\r\n\r\n## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\nFixes an issue where users sending an image through a host-mode channel could receive a text-only native-vision turn after OpenClaw staged the attachment into the agent workspace.\r\n\r\n## Why This Change Was Made\r\n\r\nHost-mode staging now carries its effective workspace root into the preparation context, allowing the existing scoped media loader to read the rewritten path. The runner context remains unchanged so the already-prepared image is not hydrated a second time. No path-validation or channel-config allowlist is widened.\r\n\r\n## User Impact\r\n\r\nNative-vision models receive one copy of the original image bytes after managed inbound media is staged into a host agent workspace.\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\n- Current `main` deterministic red: host staging succeeded, but the staged workspace was absent from the preparation context and native resolution returned zero images.\r\n- Patched green: 12/12 focused tests across host staging and current-turn image hydration.\r\n- Duplicate regression coverage exercises preparation followed by runner hydration and pins the result to one image.\r\n- `oxfmt`, `oxlint`, and `git diff --check` pass on the changed surface.\r\n- Redacted live observation:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nstaged_path=<workspace>/media/inbound/openclaw-staged-<uuid>/image.png\r\nprovider_request.imagesCount=0\r\nresolver_without_MediaWorkspaceDir=0\r\nresolver_with_MediaWorkspaceDir=1\r\n```\r\n\r\n- The first local Codex review identified a possible double-hydration path; the revised patch limits the workspace root to the preparation context and adds a regression test for exactly one image.\r\n- `pnpm check:changed` could not start locally because the Crabbox wrapper failed its CLI sanity check; repository CI remains the full-lane proof.\r\n\r\nThis PR was authored and investigated autonomously by Codex at the repository owner's request. The repository owner has not manually reviewed the code.",
